IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Kansas temporary assistance for needy families (TANF): K.S.A. 39-702, 39-709, 39-719b, 39-7,124 and 39-7,127, with the
-- payment standards of K.A.R. 30-4-100 and 30-4-101 -- the seat-neutral core.
--
-- Written in the act's own actors and terms: the "applicant" and "recipient", the "dependent child", the "family group",
-- the "secretary" (for children and families) and the "Kansas department for children and families", the "assistance
-- plan", the "basic standard" and "shelter standard".
--
-- Edition: Kansas Statutes online (Office of Revisor of Statutes, read 2026-10-20; 2025 session laws), deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/ksa-39-7-public-assistance-tanf.txt (retrieved 2026-10-19 UTC); and K.A.R. 30-4-100 and
-- 30-4-101 from the Secretary of State's 2022 Kansas Administrative Regulations, Volume 3 (regulations filed through
-- 31 December 2021), deposited in the sibling subject ../../../kansas-administrative-regulations-30-4-100-to-30-4-102-
-- tanf-payment-standards/registers/source-bundle/kar-30-4-100-to-30-4-102-tanf-payment-standards.txt.
--
-- The rules that subtract countable income from the standard (K.A.R. 30-4-110 to 30-4-113) are NOT deposited, so this
-- encoding gives the standard (the most a plan can receive), not the grant after income. NOTES.md.
--
-- The applicant's seat questions are in ks-tanf-seat.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Kansas TANF`

§§ `39-702(g) -- dependent child`

-- "'Dependent children' means needy children under the age of 18, or who are under the age of 19 and are full-time
-- students in secondary schools or the equivalent educational program who are in the care of a biological or adoptive
-- parent, court appointed guardian, conservator or legal custodian and who are living with any relative, including first
-- cousins, uncles, aunts, and persons of preceding generations ..., and including the spouses or former spouses of any
-- persons named ..., in a place of residence maintained by one or more of such relatives as their own home."
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `full-time secondary school student` IS A BOOLEAN
      `living with a relative in a home that relative maintains` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a dependent child` IF
        (`age` LESS THAN 18 OR (`age` LESS THAN 19 AND `full-time secondary school student`))
    AND `living with a relative in a home that relative maintains`

§§ `39-709(a) -- general eligibility`

-- (a)(1): "assistance ... may be granted to any needy person who: (A) Has insufficient income or resources to provide a
-- reasonable subsistence compatible with decency and health ...; (B) is a citizen of the United States or is an alien
-- lawfully admitted to the United States; and (C) resides in the state of Kansas." (a)(2): "No person who voluntarily
-- quits employment or who is fired from employment due to gross misconduct ... or who is a fugitive from justice by reason
-- of a felony conviction or charge or violation of a condition of probation or parole ... shall be eligible". Whether
-- income and resources are "insufficient" is the secretary's determination under rules not deposited: an input.
DECLARE `General eligibility facts` HAS
    `income or resources are insufficient, as the secretary determines` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a citizen or an alien lawfully admitted`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `resides in Kansas`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `voluntarily quit employment, or was fired for gross misconduct`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a fugitive from justice for a felony, or a probation or parole violation` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN g IS A `General eligibility facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the 39-709(a) general requirements` IF
        g's `income or resources are insufficient, as the secretary determines`
    AND g's `a citizen or an alien lawfully admitted`
    AND g's `resides in Kansas`
    AND (NOT g's `voluntarily quit employment, or was fired for gross misconduct`)
    AND (NOT g's `a fugitive from justice for a felony, or a probation or parole violation`)

§§ `39-709(b)(3) -- the time limit`

-- "The family group shall not be eligible for TANF if the family group contains at least one adult member who has
-- received TANF, including the federal TANF received in any other state, for 24 calendar months beginning on and after
-- October 1, 1996, unless the secretary determines a hardship exists and grants an extension allowing receipt of TANF until
-- the 36-month limit is reached. No extension beyond 36 months shall be granted." The hardships are (A) to (E).
DECLARE `Hardship` IS ONE OF
    `caretaker of a disabled family member living in the household`
    `a disability that precludes employment on a long-term basis or requires substantial rehabilitation`
    `needs an extension to overcome the effects of domestic violence or sexual assault`
    `involved with prevention and protection services with an open social service plan`
    `another extreme hardship found by the executive review team by the 24th month`
    `no hardship`

GIVEN `most months any adult in the family group has received TANF` IS A NUMBER
      `hardship` IS A `Hardship`
      `the secretary grants a hardship extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is within the time limit` IF
        `most months any adult in the family group has received TANF` LESS THAN 24
    OR  (    `most months any adult in the family group has received TANF` LESS THAN 36
         AND (NOT (`hardship` EQUALS `no hardship`))
         AND `the secretary grants a hardship extension`)

§§ `39-709(b)(8), (9) -- work participation and penalties`

-- (b)(8)(B): "(i) ... at least 30 hours of participation per week, at least 20 hours of which shall be primary ... in one
-- parent households where the youngest child is six years of age or older. (ii) Participation hours shall be 55 hours per
-- week in two parent households, 35 hours per week if child care is not used. ... (iii) ... 55 hours per week, 50 hours of
-- which shall be in primary components, or ... 35 hours per week, 30 hours of which must be primary components, if the
-- Kansas department for children and families paid child care is not received by the family. (iv) Single parent families
-- with a child under six years of age meet the federal participation requirement if the parent is engaged in work or work
-- activities for at least 20 hours per week in a primary work component."
DECLARE `Weekly participation` HAS
    `total hours`   IS A NUMBER
    `primary hours` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `two parent household` IS A BOOLEAN
      `youngest child is under six` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the family receives department-paid child care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Weekly participation`
`required weekly participation` MEANS
    IF `two parent household`
    THEN IF `the family receives department-paid child care`
         THEN `Weekly participation` WITH `total hours` IS 55, `primary hours` IS 50
         ELSE `Weekly participation` WITH `total hours` IS 35, `primary hours` IS 30
    ELSE IF `youngest child is under six`
         THEN `Weekly participation` WITH `total hours` IS 20, `primary hours` IS 20
         ELSE `Weekly participation` WITH `total hours` IS 30, `primary hours` IS 20

-- (b)(8)(D): "A parent or other adult caretaker personally providing care for a child under the age of three months in
-- their TANF household shall be exempt from work participation activities until the month the child attains three months
-- of age", not for (i) either parent in a two-parent household, (ii) one caretaker when the other is in the home and able
-- to care, (iii) a person 19 or younger without a diploma or equivalent who is pregnant or a parent, (iv) a person assigned
-- to a work activity for substance use disorders. (The premature, ill or disabled child extension is by rules of the
-- secretary, not deposited: an input.)
GIVEN `caring personally for a child under three months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child was born significantly premature, seriously ill or disabled, as the secretary defines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `two parents in the home meeting the two-parent definition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another parent or caretaker in the home is available, capable and suitable to care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `19 or younger, pregnant or a parent, without a high school diploma or equivalent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `assigned to a work activity for substance use disorders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is exempt from work participation for a young child` IF
        (`caring personally for a child under three months` OR `the child was born significantly premature, seriously ill or disabled, as the secretary defines`)
    AND (NOT `two parents in the home meeting the two-parent definition`)
    AND (NOT `another parent or caretaker in the home is available, capable and suitable to care`)
    AND (NOT `19 or younger, pregnant or a parent, without a high school diploma or equivalent`)
    AND (NOT `assigned to a work activity for substance use disorders`)

-- (b)(8)(G) work programs and (b)(9) child support services: "First penalty, three months and full cooperation ...;
-- second penalty, six months ...; third penalty, one year ...; and fourth or subsequent penalty, 10 years."
-- Returned in months; NOTHING for no penalty.
GIVEN `which penalty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`months of ineligibility for non-cooperation` MEANS
    IF `which penalty` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `which penalty` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 3
         ELSE IF `which penalty` EQUALS 2 THEN JUST 6
              ELSE IF `which penalty` EQUALS 3 THEN JUST 12
                   ELSE JUST 120

§§ `39-709(b)(5), (6) -- the work program assessment`

-- (b)(6): "During the application processing period, applicants must complete at least one module or its equivalent of
-- the work program assessment to be considered eligible for TANF benefits, unless good cause is found to be exempt",
-- with good cause "only" as (A) to (F). (b)(5): adults "not otherwise eligible ..., such as ineligible aliens,
-- relative/non-relative caretakers and adults receiving supplemental security income are not required".
DECLARE `Good cause for the assessment` IS ONE OF
    `an existing certification of completing the work program assessment`
    `a valid offer of employment, or employed at least 20 hours a week`
    `a parenting teen without a GED or high school diploma`
    `enrolled in job corps`
    `working with a refugee social services agency`
    `completed the work program assessment within the last 12 months`
    `no good cause`

GIVEN `good cause` IS A `Good cause for the assessment`
      `a caretaker who is not otherwise eligible, or receives SSI` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must complete a module of the work program assessment` IF
        (`good cause` EQUALS `no good cause`)
    AND (NOT `a caretaker who is not otherwise eligible, or receives SSI`)

§§ `39-7,124 -- a minor parent's living arrangement`

-- "(a) ... no ... grant payment shall be made on behalf of a minor under the age of 18 years who has never married and who
-- has a child or is pregnant unless such minor resides with a parent, legal guardian or other adult relative or in a
-- foster home, maternity home or other adult-supervised living arrangement." (b) exceptions: (1) no living parent or
-- guardian, or whereabouts unknown; (2) the state determines health or safety would be jeopardized; (3) lived apart from
-- the parent or guardian for at least one year before the birth or the application.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER
      `has ever married` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has a child or is pregnant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lives with a parent, guardian or other adult relative, or in an adult-supervised arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exception in 39-7,124(b) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 39-7,124 bar applies` IF
        `age` LESS THAN 18
    AND (NOT `has ever married`)
    AND `has a child or is pregnant`
    AND (NOT `lives with a parent, guardian or other adult relative, or in an adult-supervised arrangement`)
    AND (NOT `an exception in 39-7,124(b) applies`)

§§ `39-7,127 -- the work-and-earn incentive disregard`

-- (a)(1): "an incentive disregard of the amount equal to a $90 work expense plus 40% of the gross monthly earned income
-- above the $90". (b): implemented "only if such waivers to federal program requirements have been obtained".
GIVEN `gross monthly earned income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 39-7,127 earned income disregard` MEANS
    IF `gross monthly earned income` AT MOST 90
    THEN max 0 `gross monthly earned income`
    ELSE 90 PLUS (0.4 TIMES (`gross monthly earned income` MINUS 90))

GIVEN `gross monthly earned income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`earned income left after the 39-7,127 disregard` MEANS
    `gross monthly earned income` MINUS `the 39-7,127 earned income disregard` `gross monthly earned income`

§§ `K.A.R. 30-4-100, 30-4-101 -- the payment standards`

-- 30-4-101(a): "Basic standard ... $132.00 | $217.00 | $294.00 | $362.00" for 1 to 4 persons in plan; "For each
-- additional person, add $61.00." The basic standards "include $18.00 per person as an energy supplement".
GIVEN `persons in plan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the basic standard` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `persons in plan` AT MOST 0 THEN 0
        IF `persons in plan` EQUALS 1 THEN 132
        IF `persons in plan` EQUALS 2 THEN 217
        IF `persons in plan` EQUALS 3 THEN 294
        IF `persons in plan` EQUALS 4 THEN 362
        OTHERWISE 362 PLUS (61 TIMES (`persons in plan` MINUS 4))

-- 30-4-101(b): the shelter standard by county group: Group I $92, Group II $97, Group III $109, Group IV $135.
DECLARE `Shelter group` IS ONE OF `Group I`, `Group II`, `Group III`, `Group IV`

GIVEN county IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Shelter group`
`the shelter group of` county MEANS
    IF elem county (LIST "Douglas", "Harvey", "Johnson") THEN JUST `Group IV`
    ELSE IF elem county (LIST "Butler", "Jefferson", "Leavenworth", "McPherson", "Miami", "Osage", "Reno", "Rice", "Riley", "Sedgwick", "Shawnee", "Wyandotte") THEN JUST `Group III`
         ELSE IF elem county (LIST "Franklin", "Gray", "Kiowa", "Morton", "Pawnee", "Seward", "Sherman") THEN JUST `Group II`
              ELSE IF elem county (LIST "Allen", "Anderson", "Atchison", "Barber", "Barton", "Bourbon", "Brown", "Chase", "Chautauqua", "Cherokee", "Cheyenne", "Clark", "Clay", "Cloud", "Coffey", "Comanche", "Cowley", "Crawford", "Decatur", "Dickinson", "Doniphan", "Edwards", "Elk", "Ellis", "Ellsworth", "Finney", "Ford", "Geary", "Gove", "Graham", "Grant", "Greeley", "Greenwood", "Hamilton", "Harper", "Haskell", "Hodgeman", "Jackson", "Jewell", "Kearny", "Kingman", "Labette", "Lane", "Lincoln", "Linn", "Logan", "Lyon", "Marion", "Marshall", "Meade", "Mitchell", "Montgomery", "Morris", "Nemaha", "Neosho", "Ness", "Norton", "Osborne", "Ottawa", "Phillips", "Pottawatomie", "Pratt", "Rawlins", "Republic", "Rooks", "Rush", "Russell", "Saline", "Scott", "Sheridan", "Smith", "Stafford", "Stanton", "Stevens", "Sumner", "Thomas", "Trego", "Wabaunsee", "Wallace", "Washington", "Wichita", "Wilson", "Woodson") THEN JUST `Group I`
                   ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN g IS A `Shelter group`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shelter standard` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `Group I`   THEN 92
    WHEN `Group II`  THEN 97
    WHEN `Group III` THEN 109
    WHEN `Group IV`  THEN 135

-- 30-4-100(b)(1): "The basic standard and 100% of the shelter standard" where all persons in the home are in the plan, or
-- the only others are an SSI recipient with the one-third reduction, or a bona fide commercial landlord-tenant
-- relationship, or a commercial or publicly funded living arrangement. (b)(2): otherwise, when others not in the plan live
-- in the home, "a percentage reduction of the shelter standard ... (A) 60% reduction for one person in the plan; (B) 50%
-- ... two; (C) 40% ... three; (D) 35% ... four; (E) 30% ... five; and (F) 20% reduction for six or more".
GIVEN `persons in plan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the 30-4-100(b)(2) shelter reduction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `persons in plan` AT MOST 1 THEN 0.6
        IF `persons in plan` EQUALS 2 THEN 0.5
        IF `persons in plan` EQUALS 3 THEN 0.4
        IF `persons in plan` EQUALS 4 THEN 0.35
        IF `persons in plan` EQUALS 5 THEN 0.3
        OTHERWISE 0.2

GIVEN `persons in plan` IS A NUMBER
      g IS A `Shelter group`
      `others not in the plan live in the home, outside the 30-4-100(b)(1) cases` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the TANF payment standard` MEANS
    `the basic standard` `persons in plan`
        PLUS (IF `others not in the plan live in the home, outside the 30-4-100(b)(1) cases`
              THEN `the shelter standard` g TIMES (1 MINUS `the 30-4-100(b)(2) shelter reduction` `persons in plan`)
              ELSE `the shelter standard` g)

§§ `Duties: reporting changes, the assessment, using TANF`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the recipient`
    `the applicant`
    `the secretary`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `notify the secretary of the change`
    `complete a module of the work program assessment`
    `use TANF for a prohibited purchase or at a prohibited place`

-- 39-719b(a): if "the recipient ... becomes possessed of any property or income in excess of the amount ascertained at
-- the time of granting assistance, or if any of the recipient's circumstances which affect eligibility ... change ..., it
-- shall be the duty of the recipient to notify the secretary immediately". "Immediately" has no number of days; the rule
-- has no WITHIN (NOTES.md finding 5). The secretary "may, after investigation, cancel or modify the assistance payment".
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
DECIDE `the 39-719b duty to report a change` IS
    PARTY  `the recipient`
    MUST   `notify the secretary of the change`
    HENCE  FULFILLED

-- 39-709(b)(6): the module is to be completed "During the application processing period", unless good cause.
GIVEN `days in the application processing period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
DECIDE `the 39-709(b)(6) duty to complete an assessment module` IS
    PARTY  `the applicant`
    MUST   `complete a module of the work program assessment`
    WITHIN `days in the application processing period`
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "no module of the work program assessment was completed during the application processing period, and no good cause was found: the applicant is not eligible for TANF (39-709(b)(6))"

-- 39-709(b)(10): "No TANF shall be used to purchase alcohol, cigarettes, tobacco products, lottery tickets, ... No TANF
-- shall be used in any retail liquor store, casino, ... No TANF shall be used for purchases at points of sale outside the
-- state of Kansas."
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
DECIDE `the 39-709(b)(10) bar on prohibited uses of TANF` IS
    PARTY  `the recipient`
    SHANT  `use TANF for a prohibited purchase or at a prohibited place`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the recipient` BECAUSE "TANF was used for a purchase or at a place 39-709(b)(10) prohibits"
